From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:20:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 076/138] drm: adp: t7000: Freezable stall watchdog, idle
 fallback timer, stall test knob

Review fixes for the stall watchdog:

- Queue the watchdog on system_freezable_wq. During system suspend the
  IRQ line is suspended while timers and unfrozen kworkers keep running,
  so a work on system_wq declared a healthy pipe stalled. A frozen work
  first runs again after thaw, when the VBIs are back.
- The fallback hrtimer (after a storm-guard kill or a stall) only runs
  while DRM vblank is enabled: the callback returns HRTIMER_NORESTART
  when vblank is off and enable_vblank restarts it. That avoids 60 Hz
  wakeups with the screen off. It is not cancelled from disable_vblank,
  which runs under vbl_lock and the callback can reach vbl_lock through
  drm_vblank_put().
- Report the layer write as done only if the IRQ actually wrote it
  (layer_done), not by the absence of a stall.
- The watchdog's counters are reset in the work itself (enable_vblank
  only sets a flag).
- debugfs "stall": "trip" declares a stall on the next watchdog run on a
  healthy pipe, through the real stall path; "recover" undoes a watchdog
  stall (IRQ back on, timer off, watchdog rearmed). A storm-guard kill
  stays permanent.
- Record the ADBE0 frame/line register at the moment the IRQ writes
  LAYER_CTL and show it in debugfs "power", to settle where the VBI
  falls in the frame.
- Move the scanout-off comment back above its function.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/adp/adp-t7000.c | 198 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 160 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/adp/adp-t7000.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/adp/adp-t7000.c
